## 3. WHY PROVIDERS CANNOT BUILD THIS (Structural Conflict of Interest)

### 3.1 Revenue Conflict (The Maker-Checker Problem)

Cloud/AI providers face structural misalignment [K]:
- Their revenue = customer consumption. Cost optimization = cannibalizing own revenue.
- "Maker-Checker" principle: maker (provider) and checker (cost solution) CANNOT be same entity [SOURCE: Finabeo FinOps framework, 2025]
- AWS CloudWatch costs 17% MORE than third-party alternatives [SOURCE: comparative analysis, 2025]
- Native tools (AWS Cost Explorer, Azure Cost Management) "rarely offer deep allocation, meaningful business context, or multi-provider management" [K]

### 3.2 Multi-Provider Blindspot

- 76% enterprises operate across 2+ cloud providers [K, Forrester 2025]
- 37% enterprises use 5+ LLM models in production [K, typedef.ai 2026]
- Average enterprise: 4.7 models [K, Menlo Ventures 2025]
- NO provider will help customers optimize across competitors' platforms

### 3.3 Provider Native Cost Features Are Deliberately Limited

Anthropic's Enterprise Analytics API (March 2026): per-user cost attribution, 9 endpoints [K]. BUT:
- Single-provider view only (no cross-provider routing optimization)
- No multi-provider benchmark data
- No shadow AI detection across competing providers
- No cost FORECASTING with cross-vendor comparison
- No EU AI Act compliance logging (they benefit from opacity)

OpenAI: Custom invoiced pricing, even less visibility [K]

**Conclusion:** Providers will build "enough" cost visibility to RETAIN customers, never enough to help customers REDUCE spend or SWITCH. The 20-30% of value that requires cross-provider intelligence is structurally impossible for them.

