**Why it's defensible:**
- Switching FinOps platform = losing forecasting accuracy for 6+ months
- 80% of companies can't predict data-related cloud costs [K, Forrester]
- Longer history = better forecasting = higher switching cost
- Each enterprise's data is UNIQUE (their workflows, their teams, their patterns)

**Switching cost timeline:**
| Months on platform | Data value | Switching pain |
|---|---|---|
| 0-3 | Low | Easy to switch |
| 3-6 | Medium — first meaningful forecasts | Moderate friction |
| 6-12 | High — anomaly baselines established | Significant cost |
| 12-24 | Very high — year-over-year trends | Painful (lose all trend analysis) |
| 24+ | Critical — compliance audit trail | Near-impossible (EU AI Act requires 6mo+ logs) |

### 4.2 Compliance Moat: EU AI Act (August 2026)

**Hard requirements create MANDATORY demand:**
- Article 12: Automatic logging of AI system operations [K]
- Article 13: Documentation for deployers to interpret logs [K]
- Articles 19/26: 6-month MINIMUM log retention [K]
- Tamper-proof logging required (evidentiary value) [K]
- Penalty: Up to €35M or 7% worldwide turnover [K]
- 78% of organizations have NOT started compliance [K, Vision Compliance April 2026]

**Why this creates moat:**
- Once logging infrastructure established, switching = compliance gap
- Regulators can demand proof logs weren't modified
- Historical compliance trail = legal protection (can't be rebuilt)
- "Organizations that set up audit logging via AI gateway from day one build direct compliance advantage" [K, Team Rockstars IT whitepaper]

**Cost of compliance:**
- Large enterprises: $8-15M initial [K, SQ Magazine 2026]
- Mid-size: $2-5M initial, $500K-2M annual [K]
- Infrastructure cost increase: ~12% for logging/traceability [K]
- This FORCES enterprise spend on the control layer regardless of cost savings

### 4.3 Network Effects: Benchmark Intelligence

**How more customers = better product:**
- Cross-enterprise cost benchmarks ("your cost per 1K tokens is 40% above industry median")
- Model routing intelligence ("for your use-case type, Claude 4 beats GPT-5 by 23% cost-adjusted")
- Anonymous aggregate patterns = proprietary dataset no provider has
- More customers → more data → better forecasts → more customers

**Precedent:** CloudHealth (sold to VMware $200M+) built moat through multi-tenant cost benchmarks.

### 4.4 Workflow Integration Moat

